WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.860
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.130 --> 00:07.183
(We’re going to hang out after this event.)

3
00:07.398 --> 00:08.455
(Wanna join us?) NAWINA HOMECOMING

4
00:08.479 --> 00:09.679
I have somewhere I need to be.

5
00:09.844 --> 00:10.844
A funeral.

6
00:11.359 --> 00:12.999
It’s an old friend who meant a lot to me.

7
00:14.772 --> 00:16.972
There’s something I want to tell you before anyone else.

8
00:17.181 --> 00:19.720
I’ve decided not to apply to law school anymore.

9
00:20.324 --> 00:21.000
Huh?

10
00:21.087 --> 00:23.760
At first, my dad was supposed to transfer overseas for work,

11
00:24.154 --> 00:25.154
At first?

12
00:25.306 --> 00:27.640
But now I’m not moving anymore.

13
02:10.522 --> 02:13.106
(I’ve decided not to apply to law school anymore.)

14
02:13.821 --> 02:16.080
But now I’m not moving anymore.

15
02:16.850 --> 02:17.878
(Because of you.)

16
02:18.117 --> 02:20.406
- (I’ve had so much fun spending this semester with you.) - ( Because of you.)

17
02:20.430 --> 02:22.811
(You were the one who told me that if I wanted to draw, )

18
02:22.836 --> 02:23.537
(I should just do it instead of waiting.)

19
02:23.562 --> 02:24.882
Have you been studying that hard?

20
02:24.977 --> 02:26.600
You look like you didn’t get any sleep.

21
02:30.190 --> 02:31.360
I didn’t sleep very well.

22
02:31.760 --> 02:33.440
Don’t worry too much about the exams.

23
02:33.888 --> 02:35.336
It’s not that serious.

24
02:56.113 --> 02:58.200
La la

25
03:03.320 --> 03:06.160
(VEGETABLE AND FLOWER GARDEN] (HOME ECONOMICS]

26
03:07.095 --> 03:07.803
Mr. Tin.

27
03:07.903 --> 03:08.903
Hey.

28
03:09.781 --> 03:10.781
Jiraphat.

29
03:12.816 --> 03:14.456
There’s no morning assembly today, right?

30
03:14.682 --> 03:16.000
Why did you come so early?

31
03:19.741 --> 03:23.880
Is this the vegetable garden they have to finish by the end of the semester?

32
03:25.782 --> 03:26.902
Do me a favor.

33
03:27.519 --> 03:29.439
Can you keep this from the junior high students?

34
03:30.360 --> 03:33.280
You’ve been doing this every morning?

35
03:33.369 --> 03:37.160
Oh, no. We’ve been taking turns watering these plants.

36
03:37.851 --> 03:41.120
You know our school has so many activities.

37
03:41.236 --> 03:44.000
I do what I can to help the students.

38
04:04.821 --> 04:05.941
Hey, Jiraphat.

39
04:10.019 --> 04:12.200
Are you worried about Tyler and Phappim?

40
04:27.172 --> 04:31.200
Tyler’s father told me at the parent-teacher meeting

41
04:32.012 --> 04:34.532
that he would have his son withdraw at the end of this semester.

42
04:35.547 --> 04:38.120
But a few days ago, he called to tell me

43
04:38.501 --> 04:39.756
that he’d changed his mind.

44
04:41.084 --> 04:43.640
As for Phappim, after returning from the school trip,

45
04:43.844 --> 04:47.240
she asked me to talk to her family.

46
04:48.530 --> 04:49.608
But you know what?

47
04:49.730 --> 04:53.470
Both of them…mentioned you.

48
04:55.167 --> 04:56.546
So I guessed you were involved.

49
05:00.549 --> 05:01.880
What are you afraid of, Jiraphat?

50
05:06.498 --> 05:07.498
I...

51
05:07.789 --> 05:11.501
Do you really think those two will decide their own futures

52
05:12.198 --> 05:13.640
based only on what you say?

53
05:19.895 --> 05:21.000
Why worry?

54
05:21.429 --> 05:23.406
They don't even seem worried about it.

55
05:24.768 --> 05:26.440
No one knows the future.

56
05:28.754 --> 05:29.880
Someone might do.

57
05:30.352 --> 05:31.352
Hmm?

58
05:32.701 --> 05:36.400
What if the path they don't choose is the better one?

59
05:37.144 --> 05:42.200
Well, life offers a million choices.

60
05:43.283 --> 05:45.960
Even if those two really do choose the wrong path,

61
05:47.946 --> 05:49.080
would you abandon them?

62
05:52.491 --> 05:53.491
I wouldn’t.

63
05:59.405 --> 06:02.000
When I found out I’d be the advisor for Class 7,

64
06:02.406 --> 06:04.280
you were the one I was most worried about.

65
06:05.091 --> 06:06.091
Me?

66
06:06.847 --> 06:08.781
Of course. In your first semester of Grade 10,

67
06:08.806 --> 06:10.880
you were in my history class, right?

68
06:11.589 --> 06:15.880
Mr. Narong told me you were the kind of student who came late and left early.

69
06:16.554 --> 06:17.880
Never participated in activities.

70
06:18.669 --> 06:19.669
But you know what?

71
06:20.252 --> 06:21.360
In my class,

72
06:22.393 --> 06:25.000
you were the only one who always paid attention.

73
06:26.978 --> 06:29.280
And at last year’s science fair,

74
06:29.682 --> 06:33.680
I saw you cleaning up the equipment your classmates had left behind.

75
06:34.721 --> 06:38.480
So when Tyler asked me to put your name down for the offering trays,

76
06:38.888 --> 06:40.848
I wasn’t trying to make things difficult for you.

77
06:42.516 --> 06:44.440
From everything I’ve observed about you,

78
06:46.630 --> 06:48.240
I just wanted all your classmates

79
06:48.953 --> 06:50.280
to remember the name Jiraphat.

80
07:03.566 --> 07:06.360
Does that smile mean you’re not worried anymore?

81
07:07.040 --> 07:08.040
Thank you, sir.

82
07:08.204 --> 07:10.040
I’ll go then.

83
07:15.006 --> 07:16.526
Oh, wait, Jiraphat.

84
07:16.847 --> 07:17.847
Yes, sir?

85
07:17.938 --> 07:19.000
Can I ask you something?

86
07:21.760 --> 07:23.320
Are you close with the class president?

87
07:26.236 --> 07:28.680
Well…I guess I am.

88
07:29.407 --> 07:31.040
Are you dating someone?

89
07:32.041 --> 07:33.041
Huh?

90
07:34.257 --> 07:35.680
How can I be dating anyone?

91
07:37.924 --> 07:39.720
Forget it. I was just pulling your leg.

92
07:40.466 --> 07:42.003
- Good luck with your exam. - Thank you.

93
07:49.965 --> 07:50.596
Here.

94
07:50.621 --> 07:51.621
Of course.

95
07:52.027 --> 07:55.480
Damn! The exam was so freaking difficult.

96
07:55.792 --> 07:57.543
Ms. Suda must still be mad at us?

97
07:57.696 --> 07:59.298
Please give her some credit.

98
07:59.588 --> 08:01.548
Ms. Suda only made the multiple-choice questions.

99
08:01.615 --> 08:03.456
Ms. Mai is responsible for the three written-response questions.

100
08:03.480 --> 08:04.608
GRADE 11, CLASS 7 Huh?

101
08:04.777 --> 08:05.777
Really?

102
08:05.822 --> 08:09.720
Oh, so she’s not as kind as I thought.

103
08:09.951 --> 08:11.204
Let’s go play football.

104
08:11.243 --> 08:12.760
- Come on. Let’s go. - Damn it.

105
08:15.635 --> 08:17.360
Hey, you okay?

106
08:18.635 --> 08:19.635
I’m okay.

107
08:21.832 --> 08:22.960
Since we have time,

108
08:23.730 --> 08:25.360
wanna go get some egg yolk ice-cream?

109
08:26.245 --> 08:28.080
To celebrate you not moving abroad.

110
08:28.582 --> 08:29.326
Let’s go!

111
08:29.366 --> 08:30.629
- Come on, hurry. - Go then.

112
08:33.547 --> 08:34.547
Hey, Kong.

113
08:34.683 --> 08:36.720
- Hey, what’s up? - Wanna go get egg yolk ice-cream?

114
08:36.756 --> 08:37.640
Sure, why not?

115
08:37.707 --> 08:38.760
How are you doing?

116
08:38.997 --> 08:41.120
- Did you finish the exam? - It finished me.

117
08:41.237 --> 08:42.560
Hey, where are you guys going?

118
08:42.810 --> 08:44.994
- To get egg yolk ice-cream. - Hey, I’ll join you.

119
08:45.375 --> 08:46.680
Hey, Ked. Hey, Pim.

120
08:47.062 --> 08:48.360
Wanna go get egg yolk ice-cream?

121
08:48.524 --> 08:50.338
Yeah, sure. No basketball practice today.

122
08:50.369 --> 08:52.797
I’ll go, too. I don’t have extra classes today.

123
08:52.836 --> 08:55.400
Let’s go then. Are you waiting for your dads to give permission?

124
08:55.572 --> 08:56.572
Kongpob!

125
08:58.337 --> 09:00.249
First one there eats for free. Last one pays!

126
09:00.308 --> 09:02.680
- Hey, wait! - Go, go, go!

127
09:02.920 --> 09:04.280
Come on. What are you waiting for?

128
09:04.758 --> 09:05.758
Let’s go.

129
09:15.538 --> 09:19.320
The students who just finished their exams seem to be enjoying themselves.

130
09:19.928 --> 09:21.134
They’re laughing so loudly.

131
09:23.377 --> 09:26.520
Even now, after graduating, I still regret it.

132
09:27.210 --> 09:29.120
I should have had more fun back then.

133
09:40.504 --> 09:42.058
After presenting the flower garlands,

134
09:42.083 --> 09:46.323
MOTHER’S DAY CEREMONY, 2010 all mothers and student representatives from each class, please take your seats.

135
09:49.955 --> 09:50.955
What did I draw, Ji?

136
09:51.414 --> 09:53.094
- A cat. - Wrong, a bear.

137
09:54.365 --> 09:55.445
Enough with your old trick.

138
09:55.943 --> 09:57.160
And stop touching my back.

139
09:57.746 --> 09:59.953
Oh, you’re ticklish, aren’t you?

140
10:00.141 --> 10:01.592
- Take this! - Hey.

141
10:02.679 --> 10:03.770
Hey, Tyler.

142
10:03.961 --> 10:06.040
Ty, knock it off.

143
10:06.277 --> 10:07.480
Stop acting like a child.

144
10:07.505 --> 10:10.200
Please, I saw you do the same thing on Rose’s back.

145
10:10.909 --> 10:13.040
But did anyone make as much noise as you did?

146
10:14.573 --> 10:17.080
Don’t take it personally. He’s said something worse to me.

147
10:20.042 --> 10:21.162
I’m bored, Ji.

148
10:21.542 --> 10:23.062
When can we get back to our classroom?

149
10:23.785 --> 10:26.800
Soon. They’re almost finished taking pictures.

150
10:26.862 --> 10:29.950
Next is the presentation of certificates to Outstanding Mothers

151
10:29.975 --> 10:32.720
of the 2010 academic year.

152
10:33.776 --> 10:37.200
Hey, look. That’s President Ruth’s mother, Ms. Orn.

153
10:37.763 --> 10:39.716
I knew it. Even from here you can tell she’s beautiful.

154
10:39.740 --> 10:42.220
Ji, get down. I’ll take her picture for my dad. He’s a big fan.

155
10:43.272 --> 10:44.578
Is she the president’s real mom?

156
10:44.962 --> 10:47.640
My grandma said she was abandoned by her husband.

157
10:49.092 --> 10:51.732
But didn’t the president’s dad just come to school to see Ms. Suda?

158
10:54.311 --> 10:56.760
That was a long time ago, even before we were born.

159
10:58.215 --> 11:00.680
The president’s mom was a famous actress.

160
11:01.039 --> 11:02.760
But she suddenly disappeared

161
11:03.067 --> 11:04.800
for over ten years.

162
11:05.648 --> 11:09.160
She said in an interview that she left to get married and have three children.

163
11:09.904 --> 11:12.104
After that, the scandals surrounding her died down.

164
11:13.728 --> 11:16.920
I thought Ruth was an only child.

165
11:17.386 --> 11:21.240
Do you think his siblings’ names start with an ‘R’ like his?

166
11:21.829 --> 11:26.880
If that’s the case, I’ll get tongue-tied trying to say their names.

167
11:27.055 --> 11:29.538
No, his brother’s name is Khun and his sister’s name is Peach.

168
11:34.654 --> 11:37.365
Are you that close to him to know all that?

169
11:41.463 --> 11:42.595
I just saw it on the news.

170
12:01.785 --> 12:03.720
Ji, wait here. Don’t go have lunch without me.

171
12:03.794 --> 12:06.160
- I’ll be right back. - Yeah, I know. Just hurry.

172
12:10.951 --> 12:11.951
Ji?

173
12:13.203 --> 12:14.680
Ji, is that you?

174
12:15.198 --> 12:18.240
Wow, you’re all grown up now.

175
12:19.196 --> 12:22.360
Ruth never told me you go to this school, too.

176
12:22.628 --> 12:25.920
How are Jira and Mon doing? I haven’t seen them for ages.

177
12:26.779 --> 12:27.779
Hmm?

178
12:29.189 --> 12:30.189
Uh...

179
12:30.214 --> 12:31.214
Ms. Orn.

180
12:31.532 --> 12:32.560
Your ride’s here.

181
12:33.102 --> 12:35.320
Come over to my house sometime.

182
12:35.539 --> 12:37.720
Your family has helped me so much.

183
12:37.880 --> 12:38.880
Okay?

184
12:39.843 --> 12:41.440
- Yes, ma’am. - See you later.

185
12:43.090 --> 12:45.084
I’m off, Ruth. See you.

186
12:53.520 --> 12:56.560
- Why did your mom… - Ji, let’s watch a movie today.

187
12:57.408 --> 12:58.440
Oh, hey, Ruth.

188
13:00.759 --> 13:01.680
What movie?

189
13:01.730 --> 13:03.057
Are we renting one from the video store?

190
13:03.081 --> 13:04.720
No, let’s go to the cinema.

191
13:05.094 --> 13:06.300
I was gonna go with my dad

192
13:06.325 --> 13:08.520
but he was busy so I asked you instead.

193
13:11.651 --> 13:12.580
What’s the movie?

194
13:12.624 --> 13:15.560
Umm, I don’t remember the title.

195
13:15.920 --> 13:17.240
Oh, but I have the picture.

196
13:21.426 --> 13:22.480
A romantic movie?

197
13:23.783 --> 13:25.960
- Come on. Let’s go watch it. - Can I come?

198
13:26.668 --> 13:27.760
You want to see it, too?

199
13:29.012 --> 13:30.012
I do.

200
13:31.146 --> 13:32.894
Don’t you have any student council work?

201
13:32.944 --> 13:34.363
I asked someone else to handle it,

202
13:34.721 --> 13:36.800
and there’s no meeting today either.

203
13:39.039 --> 13:40.039
Okay then.

204
13:40.077 --> 13:41.077
Yes!

205
13:41.124 --> 13:42.400
I’ll go invite the others.

206
13:42.860 --> 13:44.280
Ji, hold on to Ruth.

207
13:45.274 --> 13:47.040
In case he changes his mind. I’ll be back.

208
13:52.421 --> 13:53.421
Don’t let go.

209
13:53.859 --> 13:55.000
Or I’ll change my mind.

210
14:03.584 --> 14:06.176
Hey, Tawan. Hey, Lita, wanna go see a movie?

211
14:06.471 --> 14:08.760
Sorry, man. Well...

212
14:09.972 --> 14:11.520
We're going together.

213
14:13.824 --> 14:14.713
Hey, Pim. Hey, Ked.

214
14:14.763 --> 14:16.240
I've seen it with my family.

215
14:16.300 --> 14:17.300
Me, too.

216
14:17.748 --> 14:19.788
- Hey, Kong. Let’s go see... - I hate romantic movies.

217
14:23.004 --> 14:24.760
At least there are three of us.

218
14:24.884 --> 14:26.947
- Are you sure you want to see it? - Of course, Ji.

219
14:27.173 --> 14:28.762
Don't look down on romantic movies.

220
14:28.899 --> 14:30.920
No, that's not what I meant.

221
14:31.713 --> 14:33.160
Hey, the light’s green. Let’s go.

222
14:47.070 --> 14:48.670
Why don't we use the overbridge instead?

223
14:50.884 --> 14:52.240
But this is a crosswalk.

224
14:52.439 --> 14:54.344
There are traffic lights and an officer directing traffic.

225
14:54.368 --> 14:55.568
It’s 100% safe.

226
14:56.337 --> 14:58.240
Umm, but...

227
14:59.358 --> 15:01.080
It'll be good exercise.

228
15:02.225 --> 15:03.522
Ruth is such a genius.

229
15:03.895 --> 15:04.895
Let's go.

230
15:16.626 --> 15:19.680
I'm excited. The last time I was at the cinema was during summer break.

231
15:20.247 --> 15:22.520
Me, too. I usually watch movies on Netfli...

232
15:25.330 --> 15:26.092
Net?

233
15:26.149 --> 15:27.189
Net what, Ji?

234
15:28.944 --> 15:29.944
Net cafe.

235
15:30.284 --> 15:32.520
- At a Net cafe. - Oh.

236
15:32.671 --> 15:33.791
At a Net cafe.

237
15:37.703 --> 15:38.604
It’s my dad, Ji.

238
15:38.676 --> 15:39.960
Hold on. Here, the tickets.

239
15:41.788 --> 15:42.788
Hello, Dad.

240
16:04.919 --> 16:06.240
Hello, test, test, Ji.

241
16:06.451 --> 16:08.880
My dad is free now, so he's coming after all.

242
16:09.027 --> 16:11.280
We're gonna have dinner and catch the next showing.

243
16:11.502 --> 16:13.327
You and Ruth go ahead and watch the movie together.

244
16:13.351 --> 16:15.400
I’m so sorry.

245
16:15.466 --> 16:17.440
Take the popcorn money. It's my treat.

246
16:17.488 --> 16:19.080
- That’s it. Bye-bye. - No, wait.

247
16:28.552 --> 16:30.000
- Uhh... - It's time, right?

248
16:30.697 --> 16:31.760
You're not going in?

249
16:33.403 --> 16:34.483
You still want to?

250
16:34.766 --> 16:35.766
Eh?

251
16:36.739 --> 16:38.139
Don’t you want to watch it with me?

252
16:40.216 --> 16:41.840
Yes, but...

253
16:45.835 --> 16:47.355
But what? Let's go.

254
16:59.693 --> 17:00.693
Where’s the president?

255
17:00.733 --> 17:02.320
Watching a movie with Ji.

256
17:03.007 --> 17:06.200
Here. I ran into Mr. Tin and he gave me this.

257
17:06.725 --> 17:08.440
Can you pass it to Class 7?

258
17:23.930 --> 17:25.280
Oh, by the way,

259
17:25.688 --> 17:29.168
everyone in this picture has a nickname and a real name that start with the same letter.

260
17:29.337 --> 17:31.349
Only Ruth is different.

261
17:31.746 --> 17:34.002
My name is Tawan Tontawan,

262
17:34.201 --> 17:36.134
and your name is Lita Lalita.

263
17:36.486 --> 17:38.078
The other five are the same, too.

264
17:38.644 --> 17:40.402
But Ruth Atiwitch...

265
17:43.516 --> 17:44.720
Oh, I just remembered.

266
17:44.817 --> 17:46.240
He used to go by another name.

267
17:50.791 --> 17:51.791
(Shone, )

268
17:52.992 --> 17:54.320
(I have something to tell you.)

269
17:56.413 --> 17:57.960
I really, really like you.

270
17:58.271 --> 17:59.600
It's been three years.

271
17:59.788 --> 18:02.360
I've tried everything. I've improved myself just for you.

272
18:02.668 --> 18:03.668
(I…)

273
18:04.992 --> 18:08.589
(I can't imagine having someone like that in my life.)

274
18:08.614 --> 18:10.174
(I’ve been studying hard just for you.)

275
18:10.302 --> 18:13.823
- (Someone who makes me want to be better.) - (But now I know what I should do.)

276
18:13.848 --> 18:15.790
(What I should have done a long time ago.)

277
18:16.241 --> 18:18.194
(I want to tell you in person…)

278
18:19.490 --> 18:20.666
That I like you, Shone.

279
18:32.624 --> 18:33.624
(Oh.)

280
18:34.636 --> 18:35.685
(Maybe not.)

281
18:47.677 --> 18:49.120
(You and Pin are dating.)

282
18:51.656 --> 18:52.936
(You’re perfect for each other.)

283
18:53.814 --> 18:55.014
(How adorable.)

284
19:00.200 --> 19:01.680
(I wish you both happiness.)

285
19:33.440 --> 19:34.822
LUCKY DRAW

286
19:35.371 --> 19:36.680
Boy Come on, come on.

287
19:36.880 --> 19:38.080
SCIENCE PROJECT

288
19:38.371 --> 19:40.838
Chrysanthemum tea! Chrysanthemum tea!

289
19:41.021 --> 19:43.200
Chrysanthemum tea! Chrysanthemum tea!

290
19:43.420 --> 19:46.080
Giving you refreshment and diabetes.

291
19:46.122 --> 19:47.840
Yay!

292
19:47.947 --> 19:49.122
Special price.

293
19:49.167 --> 19:51.831
First cup, five baht. The next one is 20 bath.

294
19:51.973 --> 19:53.440
Yay!

295
19:53.639 --> 19:54.639
Ugh.

296
19:54.931 --> 19:56.000
They’re driving me crazy.

297
19:56.380 --> 19:57.960
It’s okay. Let them be.

298
19:58.258 --> 20:01.720
I think since we’ve had them as promoters,

299
20:02.196 --> 20:03.440
our sales have gone up.

300
20:04.037 --> 20:05.120
- Really? - Don’t you think?

301
20:06.491 --> 20:08.691
Hey, is Ty skipping school today?

302
20:08.946 --> 20:11.267
I thought he was only taking half a day off to pick his dad up from the airport.

303
20:11.291 --> 20:13.171
I don't know. Maybe he just went straight home.

304
20:14.060 --> 20:16.860
Ji, why don't you take a break? You've been working since this morning.

305
20:17.138 --> 20:18.880
Let the others take over in the afternoon.

306
20:19.049 --> 20:20.049
It's fine.

307
20:20.519 --> 20:22.200
No, it's not.

308
20:22.441 --> 20:24.040
You seem quiet without Tyler.

309
20:24.337 --> 20:25.977
Why don't you go take a walk by yourself?

310
20:26.514 --> 20:28.080
If you don't know where to go,

311
20:28.533 --> 20:30.481
go to the president's room to get a fake wound.

312
20:40.166 --> 20:42.560
See? Your hands are tired.

313
20:43.430 --> 20:44.470
Let me do it.

314
20:45.447 --> 20:46.447
Go take a break.

315
20:48.244 --> 20:50.560
- Say 'Chrysanthemum' first. - Oh.

316
20:50.669 --> 20:52.582
- Let’s get more customers. - Okay, okay.

317
20:52.621 --> 20:54.294
Chrysanthemum tea.

318
20:54.867 --> 20:55.804
(Come on and try.)

319
20:55.831 --> 20:56.920
(Hey, you want some?)

320
21:00.173 --> 21:01.173
Jiraphat.

321
21:01.624 --> 21:03.252
You're lonely without Tyler, huh?

322
21:03.572 --> 21:05.200
Wanna go get a fake wound in my class?

323
21:06.203 --> 21:07.400
We're almost out of supplies.

324
21:07.494 --> 21:10.040
Get it before it's too late.

325
21:15.149 --> 21:16.840
I don't see the Class 1 booth.

326
21:17.067 --> 21:20.280
Our booth is in the lab on the second floor of the new building.

327
21:20.722 --> 21:21.760
Why is it there?

328
21:21.881 --> 21:24.200
What can I say? Our class is VIP.

329
21:25.241 --> 21:26.680
Just tell him the truth.

330
21:27.068 --> 21:28.535
Our materials stink like hell.

331
21:28.634 --> 21:30.720
So the teacher told us to move there.

332
21:30.873 --> 21:33.520
Don't tell him that. We'll lose a customer.

333
21:33.670 --> 21:36.500
It's not that bad, Ji. The glue just smells a bit intense.

334
21:36.590 --> 21:38.660
But I've covered it up with some spray.

335
21:38.716 --> 21:40.877
Mr. Narong's ancient flower spray?

336
21:41.261 --> 21:42.480
Ugh, Tawan.

337
21:42.758 --> 21:44.240
Stop killing my vibe.

338
21:44.943 --> 21:48.000
Just go, Ji. Let the president make you a fake wound.

339
21:48.218 --> 21:49.557
Tender hands. Excellent work.

340
21:49.637 --> 21:50.960
Guaranteed by Lita.

341
21:54.113 --> 21:55.880
Fine, I’ll go.

342
21:57.091 --> 21:58.600
Where's the lab again? Second floor?

343
22:02.071 --> 22:04.191
If you want to get a fake wound, please come this way.

344
22:07.597 --> 22:09.110
This room might smell a bit strong. FRIDAY, FEBRUARY 11

345
22:09.134 --> 22:10.320
Put the mask on.

346
22:24.019 --> 22:25.440
Hi, Ji, the good boy.

347
22:26.479 --> 22:27.480
Here to get a fake wound?

348
22:28.021 --> 22:29.021
Mmm.

349
22:29.722 --> 22:31.800
Oh, I forgot. I’m Ploy.

350
22:32.853 --> 22:33.853
Cinderella.

351
22:34.049 --> 22:35.049
Hey.

352
22:35.086 --> 22:36.098
You remember me?

353
22:36.188 --> 22:38.120
Of course. You were the star.

354
22:47.751 --> 22:49.200
Do you want to do Ji?

355
22:59.897 --> 23:01.320
The president is free now.

356
23:01.721 --> 23:04.480
You should have him do it.

357
23:05.889 --> 23:11.440
Having someone you’re close with do it might be more… comfortable, right?

358
23:20.012 --> 23:21.080
I’ll finish this one.

359
23:22.601 --> 23:23.601
Hi.

360
23:24.420 --> 23:25.420
Hi.

361
23:27.883 --> 23:28.883
Give me your hand.

362
23:30.040 --> 23:31.040
Huh?

363
23:31.238 --> 23:33.118
It’s easiest to do it on the back of your hand.

364
23:34.713 --> 23:36.000
Oh, okay.

365
23:46.967 --> 23:48.560
It shouldn’t hurt at all.

366
23:49.656 --> 23:50.840
But if it does, tell me.

367
23:51.398 --> 23:52.480
I’ll be more gentle.

368
24:50.460 --> 24:51.460
It’s done.

369
24:53.514 --> 24:54.514
Wow.

370
24:54.958 --> 24:56.078
Looks so cool.

371
24:57.508 --> 24:58.508
You like it?

372
24:58.869 --> 24:59.869
Mmm.

373
25:00.124 --> 25:01.124
Yeah.

374
25:09.486 --> 25:10.520
Wanna take a walk?

375
25:11.360 --> 25:12.360
Huh?

376
25:12.603 --> 25:13.417
You have time?

377
25:13.442 --> 25:16.040
You can take a break.

378
25:16.380 --> 25:19.415
I’ll have someone clean that up.

379
25:25.840 --> 25:27.120
SCIENCE PROJECT

380
25:34.752 --> 25:35.752
Need a hand?

381
25:39.802 --> 25:41.383
Lucky draw?

382
25:42.280 --> 25:43.360
- Wow. - Come on.

383
25:49.638 --> 25:52.000
- I give up. It’s too hard. - That’s okay.

384
25:57.591 --> 25:58.671
Are you uncomfortable?

385
25:59.236 --> 26:01.236
No, I got all this free stuff.

386
26:24.310 --> 26:25.310
Eat more.

387
26:25.963 --> 26:27.040
So you’ll grow up fast.

388
26:27.687 --> 26:28.687
Huh?

389
26:30.340 --> 26:31.400
Wanna go to other booths?

390
26:35.071 --> 26:36.320
What’s going on with him?

391
26:36.706 --> 26:37.706
The president.

392
26:37.747 --> 26:39.880
President, wanna make a gel candle?

393
26:40.090 --> 26:42.160
We’re almost out. I won’t charge you.

394
26:43.567 --> 26:45.296
Oh, don’t worry.

395
26:45.690 --> 26:49.000
I won’t charge either of you. Come take a seat.

396
26:50.093 --> 26:52.520
Sorry, these are all the materials we have left.

397
26:52.711 --> 26:55.120
Use them all you want. Come get me when you’re done.

398
26:55.556 --> 26:56.556
Thank you.

399
26:57.635 --> 26:58.635
Come on.

400
26:59.496 --> 27:00.616
Let’s do this.

401
27:03.822 --> 27:04.822
- You want more? - I’m good.

402
27:13.975 --> 27:14.975
Hey!

403
27:49.766 --> 27:51.440
They’ll take about ten minutes to set.

404
27:52.151 --> 27:54.160
Should we eat while waiting?

405
27:54.581 --> 27:56.021
I’ll have a donut.

406
28:03.983 --> 28:04.983
Is it good?

407
28:05.712 --> 28:06.880
Look at my teeth.

408
28:33.134 --> 28:34.134
Thank you.

409
28:41.182 --> 28:42.555
Mine looks terrible.

410
28:46.561 --> 28:47.681
Take this one.

411
28:48.409 --> 28:49.484
And give me yours.

412
28:50.558 --> 28:51.558
Huh?

413
29:03.008 --> 29:04.880
President, we have a meeting.

414
29:27.749 --> 29:28.749
(Oh?)

415
29:30.084 --> 29:31.960
(Maybe I’m not that naive.)

416
29:32.538 --> 29:33.538
(Maybe...)

417
29:36.257 --> 29:38.400
(I’ve known how I felt all along.)

418
29:39.750 --> 29:41.230
(I was just in denial.)

419
29:41.274 --> 29:45.000
My heart keeps calling your name

420
29:45.293 --> 29:48.040
Just hear what it says

421
29:48.143 --> 29:50.240
(The more time we spend together, )

422
29:50.538 --> 29:52.600
(the clearer everything is.)

423
29:53.467 --> 29:55.000
Right now

424
29:55.240 --> 29:57.760
Just having you to love is all I need

425
29:58.070 --> 29:59.697
I won’t ask for more

426
29:59.722 --> 30:02.800
Your eyes on mine, your hand in mine

427
30:02.885 --> 30:07.800
Your face always there in my sight

428
30:09.632 --> 30:13.360
Grade 11, you have to attend the sports day meeting. Don’t leave yet.

429
30:15.542 --> 30:16.840
Don’t go home yet.

430
30:17.788 --> 30:21.402
- When will this year end? - Keep your thoughts to yourselves.

431
30:21.518 --> 30:28.040
AHHHHH!

432
30:31.862 --> 30:34.608
(Somebody, help Jiraphat!)

433
30:35.013 --> 30:37.240
(Tyler, help me!)

434
30:38.238 --> 30:39.238
- Ji! - Jeez.

435
30:39.997 --> 30:41.320
You scared me.

436
30:42.385 --> 30:44.200
What were you dreaming about?

437
30:44.713 --> 30:45.746
Should we just go home?

438
30:45.775 --> 30:46.775
No, we can’t.

439
30:46.840 --> 30:48.680
I heard Ji calling out my name in my dream.

440
30:48.993 --> 30:51.293
Ji must be so lonely right now without me.

441
30:51.584 --> 30:53.160
Hurry up, dad. Take me to school now!

442
30:55.269 --> 30:56.269
Ji.

443
30:57.037 --> 30:59.640
Who dared hurt my Ji like this?

444
31:02.709 --> 31:03.920
It’s a fake wound.

445
31:04.213 --> 31:05.384
Stop being silly.

446
31:07.586 --> 31:08.800
It smells really bad, Ji.

447
31:09.527 --> 31:11.567
Are you sure it’s a fake wound and not a rotten one?

448
31:11.769 --> 31:13.120
Ruth did this for me.

449
31:13.648 --> 31:15.320
It can’t be something dangerous.

450
31:15.566 --> 31:17.360
Ruth is the most dangerous one.

451
31:17.581 --> 31:18.760
- What’d you say? - Nothing.

452
31:18.980 --> 31:20.440
Let’s clean up our booth, Ji.

453
31:20.465 --> 31:21.865
We’ll have to go to the sports day meeting next.

454
31:21.889 --> 31:22.889
Go, go, go.

455
31:22.984 --> 31:23.984
Let’s go.

456
31:24.040 --> 31:25.320
We’re here to help.

457
31:25.636 --> 31:27.400
Oh, how nice of you.

458
31:27.507 --> 31:29.446
If you’re gonna come this late, why don’t you come tomorrow?

459
31:29.470 --> 31:31.537
Please, you’re making me blush.

460
31:31.823 --> 31:33.829
- Lift it up, 1…2… - 1... 2...

461
31:34.786 --> 31:35.899
- It’s not moving, Gun. - No, no.

462
31:35.923 --> 31:37.400
- Why are you pushing it down? - Why are you doing that?

463
31:37.424 --> 31:38.424
Oh, I’m so, so sorry.

464
31:38.489 --> 31:39.827
- Again, 1... 2... 3. - Go, 1... 2... 3.

465
31:42.746 --> 31:44.924
Why are you lifting it with one hand but pushing it down with the other?

466
31:44.948 --> 31:45.670
- Yeah. - Oh, right.

467
31:45.695 --> 31:46.880
1…2…3!

468
31:51.779 --> 31:54.086
Why do I feel like you two aren’t helping?

469
31:54.569 --> 31:56.686
- Are you messing with me? - You’re just weak, Gun.

470
31:56.711 --> 31:57.442
Are you messing with me?

471
31:57.480 --> 31:58.920
Everyone, wake up.

472
31:59.078 --> 32:00.649
May I have your attention?

473
32:01.007 --> 32:02.920
Pinch your friends who are sleepy.

474
32:03.690 --> 32:06.720
For the sports day next semester,

475
32:07.282 --> 32:09.920
Grade 11 students…have to do everything.

476
32:14.712 --> 32:15.712
Quiet.

477
32:18.988 --> 32:21.880
Each class, send someone to draw a team color.

478
32:22.706 --> 32:23.706
Class 1.

479
32:27.697 --> 32:29.000
Class 1, blue.

480
32:30.167 --> 32:31.430
Ji, which team color do you want?

481
32:31.454 --> 32:32.968
I don’t think there’s a difference.

482
32:33.270 --> 32:35.400
Oh, that’s not fun. Pick one color.

483
32:35.913 --> 32:36.913
Just one.

484
32:37.634 --> 32:38.634
Then…

485
32:39.861 --> 32:41.750
I’ll choose the same color as Kongpob’s class.

486
32:42.066 --> 32:43.200
Kongpob’s class?

487
32:43.768 --> 32:44.640
Class 9?

488
32:44.783 --> 32:45.783
Mmm.

489
32:45.860 --> 32:47.820
Don’t you want to be in the same team as Class 1?

490
32:49.397 --> 32:51.160
- Gotcha! - Gotcha!

491
32:51.387 --> 32:53.280
There’re only two classes with the same color.

492
32:53.399 --> 32:55.749
- It can’t be that much of a coincidence, can it? - (Class 6, red.)

493
32:55.773 --> 32:56.773
Who knows?

494
33:00.190 --> 33:01.406
Class 7, blue.

495
33:01.431 --> 33:02.431
Hey, Ji.

496
33:02.970 --> 33:05.130
We got the same color as Ruth, Tawan, and Lita’s class.

497
33:05.589 --> 33:07.400
Are you sad?

498
33:07.999 --> 33:11.280
- That you’re not on the same team as Kongpob. - Yeah, right.

499
33:11.324 --> 33:13.960
But at least you have your best friend Ruth on your team.

500
33:14.287 --> 33:15.287
That’s nice, huh?

501
33:15.314 --> 33:16.314
Right, Ji?

502
33:21.824 --> 33:22.840
What’s the matter?

503
33:23.372 --> 33:24.381
Aren’t you happy?

504
33:25.081 --> 33:26.081
Yeah.

505
33:29.847 --> 33:32.040
Too bad we’re not on the same team.

506
33:32.420 --> 33:33.940
I’m lucky I don’t have you on my team.

507
33:36.639 --> 33:37.639
That’s hurtful.

508
33:38.084 --> 33:39.960
Now you have to buy me egg yolk ice-cream.

509
33:40.173 --> 33:40.786
Why should I?

510
33:40.829 --> 33:43.294
- I think the shop has closed by now. - No way.

511
33:43.319 --> 33:45.320
Let’s have shaved ice across the street then.

512
33:45.867 --> 33:46.867
Your treat.

513
33:47.358 --> 33:48.800
Tyler, Kongpob.

514
33:49.503 --> 33:50.503
Yes?

515
33:50.589 --> 33:51.589
What?

516
34:03.822 --> 34:04.822
What is it?

517
34:08.624 --> 34:11.040
- What if… - That means it’s a real story.

518
34:11.272 --> 34:13.440
Hey, Kong. Don’t interrupt him.

519
34:13.510 --> 34:14.510
Let him finish.

520
34:18.301 --> 34:20.120
Fine. It’s a real story.

521
34:22.014 --> 34:24.322
What would you say if I told you I’m…

522
34:27.311 --> 34:29.280
not interested in the opposite sex?

523
34:31.714 --> 34:33.960
Are you saying you like boys?

524
34:35.776 --> 34:36.960
You can say that.

525
34:38.659 --> 34:40.179
So you just wanted to ask us directly?

526
34:40.353 --> 34:42.433
You learned how to be direct from Tyler, didn’t you?

527
34:42.728 --> 34:45.480
I only asked because it’s the two of you.

528
34:53.400 --> 34:55.480
Let’s go get shaved ice.

529
34:56.526 --> 34:57.526
Hold on.

530
34:57.706 --> 34:58.746
What now, Ji?

531
34:58.844 --> 35:00.560
Let’s go before the shop closes.

532
35:00.693 --> 35:01.960
You guys are okay with that?

533
35:03.774 --> 35:05.120
Okay with what?

534
35:05.342 --> 35:06.460
Why does it matter?

535
35:07.458 --> 35:08.800
I love my dad so much, Ji.

536
35:09.829 --> 35:11.880
What does your dad have to do with this?

537
35:12.730 --> 35:15.360
Well…I was raied by two dads.

538
35:16.980 --> 35:20.960
My mom and Dad Yai got divorced when I was one year old.

539
35:21.710 --> 35:24.480
And a few years ago, before I moved to Thailand,

540
35:24.896 --> 35:26.960
Dad Yai had just legally married Dad Jiew.

541
35:32.633 --> 35:34.520
I’ve never told you that?

542
35:34.956 --> 35:36.240
No, you haven’t.

543
35:37.971 --> 35:39.320
That’s what you worry about?

544
35:40.858 --> 35:43.240
I don’t have a problem with that, personally.

545
35:43.663 --> 35:47.920
But you don’t need to tell everyone that.

546
35:48.549 --> 35:49.549
I know.

547
35:50.157 --> 35:52.680
Yay! Now that we got that out of the way,

548
35:52.839 --> 35:54.479
let’s go get some shaved ice, my friends.

549
35:54.685 --> 35:55.611
Let’s go!

550
35:55.700 --> 35:57.760
- Let’s go get shaved ice. - Let’s go.

551
35:59.977 --> 36:02.160
Hey, I know, Ji.

552
36:03.990 --> 36:04.990
Know what?

553
36:05.379 --> 36:06.760
It’s Ruth, right?

554
36:08.971 --> 36:10.600
I’m not dumb, Ji.

555
36:11.417 --> 36:12.640
Ruth is nice.

556
36:13.237 --> 36:15.217
He’s smart. We can copy his homework.

557
36:15.776 --> 36:18.120
But today he hurt you while I was away.

558
36:18.570 --> 36:19.570
That’s not cool.

559
36:21.747 --> 36:22.880
Let’s go get shaved ice.

560
36:24.014 --> 36:25.374
Mali, be careful.

561
36:25.480 --> 36:27.920
Can you lift the left side up a little bit?

562
36:29.504 --> 36:30.760
Make sure it’s level.

563
36:34.483 --> 36:35.320
Good evening, Mom.

564
36:35.364 --> 36:36.520
Good evening.

565
36:37.385 --> 36:40.025
Why didn’t you sleep at school if you’re gonna come home this late?

566
36:42.542 --> 36:43.542
What’s that?

567
36:43.653 --> 36:44.653
My gift?

568
36:48.626 --> 36:50.280
Eww, what’s this rubbish?

569
36:50.509 --> 36:51.760
Why is it so messed up?

570
36:54.294 --> 36:54.970
Oops.

571
36:55.062 --> 36:56.320
Ahem, mmm.

572
36:56.638 --> 36:59.722
So cute. It’s the cutest thing I’ve ever seen.

573
36:59.897 --> 37:01.840
Looks like it’s from the future.

574
37:03.153 --> 37:04.153
- Mom. - Hmm?

575
37:04.361 --> 37:06.640
Tawan and Lita are having dinner here today.

576
37:06.932 --> 37:10.805
- We have a meeting about the sports day. - Sure. I had the staff prepare lots of food.

577
37:14.499 --> 37:16.160
So, what do you think?

578
37:16.606 --> 37:18.320
Your dad won this painting at an auction.

579
37:18.636 --> 37:20.837
The artist who painted it has a son

580
37:20.862 --> 37:22.270
who goes to your school.

581
37:22.336 --> 37:24.680
His name is Tyler. Do you know him?

582
37:24.731 --> 37:26.440
Yes, he’s in the same class as Ji.

583
37:27.299 --> 37:28.299
Ji?

584
37:28.534 --> 37:30.200
Ji goes to your school, too?

585
37:30.633 --> 37:32.680
Why don’t you tell me? I’d love to see Jean again.

586
37:34.344 --> 37:35.880
Invite them for dinner sometime.

587
37:35.924 --> 37:37.040
Invite their whole family.

588
37:37.616 --> 37:40.840
- But what about dad? - Mmm.

589
37:41.409 --> 37:43.440
Forget that crazy old man.

590
37:43.516 --> 37:45.158
I don’t know why he’s so arrogant.37.59

591
37:59.326 --> 38:01.680
Kong, will you help me with my report?

592
38:01.847 --> 38:04.280
What? I’ll go home right after I finish dinner here.

593
38:04.787 --> 38:06.400
What do you guys think this place is?

594
38:07.006 --> 38:08.046
A place to play with Mhee.

595
38:08.162 --> 38:09.962
A place to play video games and watch movies.

596
38:10.224 --> 38:11.800
That’s it. No movies today.

597
38:11.825 --> 38:13.320
Or I won’t finish my report.

598
38:14.844 --> 38:17.600
Let’s do something fun then.

599
38:19.299 --> 38:20.320
What’s wrong with you?

600
38:21.440 --> 38:24.120
I heard that the house next door is abandoned, right?

601
38:24.709 --> 38:25.840
How about a ghost hunt?

602
38:30.926 --> 38:32.680
That’s ridiculous.

603
38:33.334 --> 38:37.200
We’re gonna end up at the police station instead for trespassing.

604
38:38.478 --> 38:40.158
You don’t have the guts.

605
38:40.203 --> 38:41.637
If you want to go on a ghost hunt,

606
38:41.798 --> 38:44.398
let’s check out the abandoned house in the alley that burned down.

607
38:45.658 --> 38:47.456
Cool! Let’s go.

608
38:48.393 --> 38:51.560
If you’re not getting in, I’m gonna close the gate.

609
38:51.590 --> 38:54.520
- I’m gonna close the gate. - Hey, hold on, hold on.

610
38:55.146 --> 38:55.892
Hey, hey, hey. Wait!

611
38:55.917 --> 38:57.557
- My shoes, my shoes. - Take your shoes off.

612
38:58.559 --> 39:00.200
Hey, wait.

613
39:00.333 --> 39:01.600
Why are you here?

614
39:01.643 --> 39:04.440
Eh? It’s my house, too. Why can’t I be here?

615
39:04.562 --> 39:07.000
- Good evening. - Good evening, beautiful Jean.

616
39:07.711 --> 39:08.751
Good evening.

617
39:08.824 --> 39:11.560
Ji, you should take him as an example.

618
39:11.790 --> 39:14.273
Stop being rude and be nicer to me.

619
39:14.296 --> 39:15.296
Here we go again.

620
39:15.713 --> 39:16.840
Hello, kids.

621
39:17.417 --> 39:18.823
- Hello, Mom. - Good evening.

622
39:18.873 --> 39:20.360
Why are you back so early?

623
39:20.451 --> 39:22.640
- Dinner isn’t ready yet. - It’s okay, ma’am.

624
39:22.752 --> 39:24.240
It’ll be worth the wait.

625
39:24.299 --> 39:26.560
That’s so nice of you, Ty.

626
39:26.669 --> 39:28.040
I’ll make you some cocoa.

627
39:28.104 --> 39:29.146
Can you make that two, please?

628
39:29.170 --> 39:30.664
I’ll make that three.

629
39:30.689 --> 39:32.080
Yes, three.

630
39:32.230 --> 39:35.360
Would you like your usual less-sweet cocoa, Kong?

631
39:35.483 --> 39:36.094
Yes, ma’am.

632
39:36.119 --> 39:37.960
- Take care of your friends. - Okay, Mom.

633
39:39.512 --> 39:41.120
Will you drink all three cups?

634
39:41.201 --> 39:42.400
It’s just three cups, Ji.

635
39:48.768 --> 39:50.000
- Here. - Thank you, ma’am.

636
39:50.122 --> 39:52.040
Your cocoa is the best in the world.

637
39:52.141 --> 39:53.640
Oh, you’re so nice.

638
39:53.822 --> 39:55.920
But I won’t make you another cup.

639
39:56.126 --> 39:59.280
You shouldn’t have too much sugar. Save some space for dinner.

640
40:00.184 --> 40:01.847
Jean, when we go to the mall tomorrow,

641
40:01.872 --> 40:04.533
remind me to buy more cocoa powder and coffee cups.

642
40:05.328 --> 40:07.728
- Okay. - We’re running out of cocoa powder.

643
40:07.805 --> 40:11.280
- You remind me of young Ji. - Jean, go help mom in the kitchen.

644
40:11.593 --> 40:13.440
No, I won’t. Why don’t you help her?

645
40:14.617 --> 40:15.657
If you won’t,

646
40:16.011 --> 40:17.880
I’ll tell mom about Dennis.

647
40:18.216 --> 40:19.216
Hey!

648
40:22.987 --> 40:25.000
- I hope Mhee bites you in the butt. - Go on.

649
40:26.168 --> 40:27.960
Ty, excuse me.

650
40:28.381 --> 40:29.381
Please.

651
40:31.112 --> 40:32.112
Bye.

652
40:33.527 --> 40:35.480
Should we watch a movie while we wait?

653
40:35.983 --> 40:37.160
Hmm? What movie?

654
40:37.202 --> 40:38.560
We didn’t rent any.

655
40:38.758 --> 40:40.695
We can find one here.

656
40:41.596 --> 40:43.960
Those are my dad’s old movies.

657
40:44.137 --> 40:46.556
They’re so old you won’t find them entertaining.

658
40:46.586 --> 40:49.000
Yes, I will. They’re classic.

659
40:49.291 --> 40:50.198
Let me dig up one.

660
40:50.223 --> 40:51.223
Hey, wait.

661
40:51.957 --> 40:52.957
Oh, sh♪t!

662
41:00.123 --> 41:02.820
- I’m sorry. - You sure are.

663
41:02.863 --> 41:04.080
Put them back now.

664
41:11.322 --> 41:12.480
What’s this, Ji?

665
41:14.451 --> 41:15.840
Looks like a photo album.

666
41:20.273 --> 41:21.273
Wow.

667
41:21.708 --> 41:22.800
If that’s Ji,

668
41:22.924 --> 41:25.640
this must be Jean, right?

669
41:25.967 --> 41:27.920
So beautiful. Ji looks cute, too.

670
41:27.993 --> 41:29.171
That’s enough, Tyler.

671
41:29.196 --> 41:30.080
Wait, Ji.

672
41:30.105 --> 41:32.320
- I don’t get to see this often. - Hey, stop it.

673
41:32.403 --> 41:33.840
- Hey, Ji. - Put it back.

674
41:34.197 --> 41:35.197
What’s that?

675
41:35.572 --> 41:36.572
What?

676
41:39.545 --> 41:40.600
Hey, let me see.

677
41:42.998 --> 41:43.998
Huh?

678
41:44.231 --> 41:47.000
Is this Ms. Ornrampha?

679
41:48.118 --> 41:49.560
How do you know her, Ji?

680
41:53.273 --> 41:55.960
How are we supposed to find anything in all these documents?

681
41:56.108 --> 41:57.040
Just keep looking.

682
41:57.116 --> 41:59.400
Last year’s records should be somewhere around here.

683
42:00.007 --> 42:00.760
Here.

684
42:00.818 --> 42:02.240
What? Did you find it?

685
42:03.072 --> 42:04.480
No, but I found this.

686
42:05.769 --> 42:06.800
What’s that?

687
42:06.904 --> 42:08.280
It’s not what we’re looking for.

688
42:08.633 --> 42:09.800
Look closely.

689
42:14.881 --> 42:16.840
Oh, this is…

690
42:17.844 --> 42:20.080
Wait, mom, come here.

691
42:21.924 --> 42:24.720
This is the photo I’ve been looking for.

692
42:25.278 --> 42:28.040
I told my friends I know Ms. Orn personally.

693
42:28.194 --> 42:29.720
But no one believed me.

694
42:29.899 --> 42:31.760
I’ll show them this picture.

695
42:31.917 --> 42:35.047
I was wondering where this photo album went.

696
42:35.513 --> 42:37.560
There’s something written in the back.

697
42:39.296 --> 42:40.600
Hey, Ji.

698
42:41.160 --> 42:44.520
MR. JIRA, MS. NARUMON, MS. ORNRAMPHA JITRADA, JIRAPHAT, THEERARUTH, IRIN

699
42:44.544 --> 42:46.412
Dinner’s ready. Let’s eat first

700
42:46.437 --> 42:47.637
and then we’ll…

701
43:25.692 --> 43:28.400
(Hold my hand. Don’t let go.)

702
43:47.122 --> 43:48.643
(I don’t know what happened.)

703
43:49.376 --> 43:51.127
(I don’t know how I traveled back in time.)

704
43:54.440 --> 43:57.480
STUDENT COUNCIL, NAWINA SCHOOL Class 7 won’t hand in their trays, right?

705
43:58.239 --> 44:01.120
(And it seems like Jiraphat)

706
44:01.799 --> 44:03.360
(has traveled back in time as well)

707
44:04.763 --> 44:06.640
You guys go ahead.

708
44:07.250 --> 44:08.400
I have to finish something.

709
44:09.210 --> 44:10.012
See you.

710
44:10.084 --> 44:11.520
(I’ll take this opportunity)

711
44:15.186 --> 44:17.880
(to do what my heart desires.)

712
44:32.892 --> 44:34.160
(And I won’t let Jiraphat)

713
44:35.747 --> 44:37.080
(end up the same way again.)

714
45:03.459 --> 45:04.819
I know the truth.

715
45:06.415 --> 45:07.415
The truth?

716
45:10.576 --> 45:13.560
(Maybe I didn't travel back in time to make new memories, )

717
45:13.656 --> 45:15.480
(or simply to remember things before I die, )

718
45:16.441 --> 45:19.951
(but to remember old memories I'd long forgotten.)
